Ability to mark a single item in a union type as deprecated in openapi spec.


```python
from fastapi import FastAPI

app = FastAPI()

@app.get("/{uuid_or_str}")
def fetch(uuid_or_str: UUID | str):
    return {"hello": "world"}
```




Using a path parameter with simple type union, I can not see if there is any way to flag one of the types as deprecated.

This is a valid api definition in openapi spec that I am attempting to replicate purely with FastAPI.

```
          "schema": {
            "oneOf": [
              {
                "type": "string",
                "title": "Code",
              },
              {
                "type": "string",
                "format": "uuid",
                "title": "ID",
                "deprecated": true,              }
            ],
          },
          "name": "uuid_or_str",
          "in": "path"
        }
